  "main_text": "<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is mia_garcia_4516 and they want to return all items ordered. They have two payment methods and two orders, and they want to refund each order to the other's payment method. If that's not possible, they get angry and then agree to use the original payment method.\n\nFirst, I need to get the user's details to see their orders and payment methods. So I should call get_user_details with their user ID. Once I have that info, I can check the orders and payment methods. \n\nThe user has two orders. For each order, they want the refund to go to the other order's payment method. But according to the policy, returns must refund to the original payment method or an existing gift card. So if the payment methods are different, like one is a credit card and the other is a gift card, maybe it's possible if the gift card is an existing one. But if both are credit cards, maybe not. \n\nI need to check the payment methods available for the user. Once I have the details, I can see if the requested refunds are possible. If not, I have to inform them and proceed with the original payment method. \n\nSo next step is to get the user's details. Let's call get_user_details with the user ID.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"get_user_details\", \"arguments\": {\"user_id\": \"mia_garcia_4516\"}}\n",
